#: ../../technical/articles/084-cross-period-checks-verification-reports-and-work-addressing.md:12
msgid "Capabilities and mechanisms"
msgstr "Képességek és mechanizmusok"

#: ../../technical/articles/084-cross-period-checks-verification-reports-and-work-addressing.md:14
msgid ""
"Cross-period verification evaluates dependencies declared by the selected"
" registry revision against prior observations, filing records, "
"calculation revisions, verification reports and justificantes. It "
"projects profile member rosters into a common dependency contract, and "
"can narrow economic-activity-conditional sources only when profile "
"applicability is positively resolved; errors or indeterminate "
"applicability suppress nothing. Explicitly attested M111 no-retenciones "
"periods are recognized as a separate no-obligation case. A helper can "
"also derive zero-valued prior-filing overrides from the target revision's"
" binding overrides. Registry-driven clean-state resolution "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/verification_cross_period.py`), fail-"
"closed conditional applicability "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/verification_cross_period.py`), zero "
"prior-filing values "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/verification_cross_period.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/084-cross-period-checks-verification-reports-and-work-addressing.md:16
msgid ""
"Each unclean dependency produces a blocking finding with the source "
"model, period, dependency origin and blocker codes, plus legal and source"
" references. Nonblocking advisories disclose operator-declared activity-"
"start suppressions, first-year Modelo 202 fractional suppressions, "
"nonofficial same-year local chains, explicitly zero prior filings, M111 "
"no-retenciones claims, and dependencies on models the taxpayer does not "
"file. When evidence is missing and no activity-start date is recorded, "
"the gate adds a second blocker asking for that date so it can distinguish"
" a true first filer from an omitted prior filing. A Modelo 303 IVA carry "
"can be covered only by a matching, unblocked wallet decision with a "
"selected amount and an allowed authority/source pair. Finding "
"construction and first-filer rule "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/verification_cross_period.py`), wallet "
"decision correlation "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/verification_cross_period.py`), blocking"
" gate (`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/verification_cross_period.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/084-cross-period-checks-verification-reports-and-work-addressing.md:18
msgid ""
"Registry-authored verification predicates provide reusable cross-casilla "
"and profile checks. Blocking operators cover nonzero requirements, "
"exclusivity, caps, equality and printed totals, implications, required "
"profile fields, and roll-forward balances with a one-cent tolerance. "
"Advisory operators cover ratios, profile flags, positive values, "
"mismatches, date-based eligibility cues and computed-versus-declared "
"divergence. Inputs and legal grounding come from the selected registry "
"revision; the evaluator retains generic operators rather than hard-coding"
" declaration facts. A malformed/unrecognized expression currently "
"evaluates as satisfied for blocking predicates and false for advisories, "
"relying on registry authoring validation to prevent invalid patterns from"
" reaching runtime. That is a concrete boundary to keep intact in any "
"alternate registry-loading path. Blocking DSL "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/verification_predicates.py`), advisory "
"DSL (`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/verification_predicates.py`), "
"registry predicate dispatch "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/verification_predicates.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/084-cross-period-checks-verification-reports-and-work-addressing.md:20
msgid ""
"Verification findings are paired with typed, locale-neutral precondition "
"identities by constructor identity rather than rendered message text. The"
" DTO validators require every blocking finding to carry exactly one "
"verify-leaf precondition, reject preconditions on warnings, and preserve "
"report finding order. A separate snapshot schema carries the complete "
"verification report, scalar-typed facts, publication state and recovery "
"decisions without widening decimals or converting recovery arguments into"
" executable commands. Precondition/result invariants "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/verification_preconditions.py`), "
"identity-based projection "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/verification_preconditions.py`), "
"canonical verification snapshot "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/verification_projection.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/084-cross-period-checks-verification-reports-and-work-addressing.md:22
msgid ""
"Two registered report-read operations expose a profile's verification "
"history or one report. They validate canonical periods, UTC timestamps, "
"unique/sorted facts and references, grant/completeness consistency and "
"exact report-to-revision/work-unit coordinates. The operations refuse "
"oversized records instead of clipping facts: limits bound rows, findings,"
" casillas, facts, references, decimal range and the final serialized "
"result. They capture the result in worker-owned custody, use credential-"
"free requests, and authorize an unfiltered profile-wide list separately "
"from a period-filtered list or single-report read. Bounded report "
"projection "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/verification_report_read_operation.py`),"
" profile/revision binding and report capture "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/verification_report_read_operation.py`),"
" list and view capture "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/verification_report_read_operation.py`),"
" period-derived access "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/verification_report_read_operation.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/084-cross-period-checks-verification-reports-and-work-addressing.md:24
msgid ""
"The withholding-detail gate handles a specific false-zero risk in annual "
"summaries. When calculation persisted an empty per-perceptor store, the "
"gate requires taxpayer attestations for every quarterly window of the "
"relevant periodic source; only M111 currently has an attestation channel."
" It also checks whether received invoices show withholding liability or "
"outgoing activity-category ledger rows show that a renta was satisfied. "
"Recorded evidence defeats an absence attestation. Proven and "
"uncontradicted absence remains a warning in the report; unproven or "
"contradicted absence blocks verification. The gate explicitly does not "
"reconcile a store that has some records but fewer than the ledger "
"evidence, so callers must not treat this check as general store "
"completeness. Absence classification "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/withholding_detail_gate.py`), finding "
"severity and provenance "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/withholding_detail_gate.py`), append to "
"verification "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/withholding_detail_gate.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/084-cross-period-checks-verification-reports-and-work-addressing.md:26
msgid ""
"Wizard operations turn the canonical calculation path into an interactive"
" flow. A private context read discovers remaining input steps for an "
"exact active work unit and selected language. A recorded attempt invokes "
"normal preparation and calculation; only the typed prepublication "
"missing-binding refusal can become a `needs_input` result, and the "
"returned step must identify that same binding with legal and source "
"grounding. Other errors propagate. Before calculation, it marks the "
"effect `UNKNOWN` because preparation may already have written migrations "
"or IVA decisions; it reports `UPDATED` only when a revision was "
"published. Cancellation is awaited around the irreversible section, and "
"results remain profile-bound. Attempt outcomes and executor "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/wizard_attempt_operation.py`), "
"calculation/effect handling "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/wizard_attempt_operation.py`), private "
"wizard discovery "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/wizard_context_operation.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/084-cross-period-checks-verification-reports-and-work-addressing.md:28
msgid ""
"Work addressing centralizes natural filing coordinates and exact IDs for "
"CLI/TUI callers. A visible target is model/year/period with an optional "
"registry-revision assertion; exact work-unit and calculation-revision "
"identifiers remain advanced paths. Natural targets are checked against "
"one law-selected registry capture, with both requested and stored "
"revision assertions independently compared to that same capture. The "
"authority grade is only applicability at creation/addressing time; "
"filing-grade checks remain later gates. Existing active work can be "
"reused after profile-readiness validation; a new one uses the law-"
"determined revision and rejects superseded census models. Law-selected "
"revision assertion (`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/work_addressing.py`),"
" reuse/create behavior "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/work_addressing.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/084-cross-period-checks-verification-reports-and-work-addressing.md:30
msgid ""
"For consistent selection under concurrent updates, capture reads a "
"versioned work-unit catalogue and, for implicit active-profile "
"addressing, fingerprints the profile pointer before and after the "
"catalogue read. A pointer change retries up to eight times. Captures "
"receive an opaque same-process comparison domain and generation; later "
"coordinates detect a superseding observation while hiding storage paths "
"and keys. Verify, file and export apply distinct revision policies: "
"verify permits an idempotent sealed-state retry for the verification "
"action to resolve, file requires `VERIFICADO_COMPLETO`, and export "
"accepts only current sealed states. Capture/current-coordinate contract "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/work_addressing.py`), capture and "
"recheck (`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/work_addressing.py`), "
"verify/file/export resolution "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/work_addressing.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/084-cross-period-checks-verification-reports-and-work-addressing.md:32
msgid "Knowledge, safety, and implementation assessment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/084-cross-period-checks-verification-reports-and-work-addressing.md:34
msgid ""
"These files rely on pinned registry authority, profile records and "
"explicitly persisted filing, ledger and operator evidence. They do not "
"establish current legal correctness; legal references and registry facts "
"are inputs that must be validated elsewhere. Strong controls include "
"fail-closed applicability, typed blocker identities, exact profile and "
"revision correlation, result-size refusal, opaque process-local capture "
"coordinates, retry on pointer/catalogue races and narrow handling of "
"missing wizard input. No external network or LLM behavior appears here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/084-cross-period-checks-verification-reports-and-work-addressing.md:36
msgid ""
"The cross-period helper returns `None` when its calculation-grade "
"registry snapshot cannot be resolved, which yields no findings from that "
"helper alone. In the normal verification flow, the filing-grade snapshot "
"is resolved earlier, but direct callers of the generic gate must preserve"
" that prerequisite. Predicate evaluation also depends on registry "
"authoring validation because unknown blocking syntax is treated as "
"holding. The report projections contain detailed finding facts, including"
" identifiers and monetary values; the surrounding access resolver scopes "
"them by profile and period, but result custody, frontend disclosure and "
"audit retention need adapter-level review. No assigned tests were "
"present, so race handling, output custody, repository behavior and "
"predicate validation were not executed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/084-cross-period-checks-verification-reports-and-work-addressing.md:38
msgid "Dependencies and follow-up"
msgstr "Függőségek és további vizsgálatok"

#: ../../technical/articles/084-cross-period-checks-verification-reports-and-work-addressing.md:40
msgid ""
"Synthesis should connect the cross-period checks to the generic clean-"
"state evaluator and its repository implementations; verify that every "
"caller resolves a mandatory snapshot before invoking the nullable helper;"
" and confirm registry build validation on all supported authority-loading"
" paths. It should also trace report-read capabilities through the "
"operation owner and encrypted operand store, and relate the wizard's "
"`UNKNOWN`/`UPDATED` effects to preparation-side writes. Work addressing "
"depends on the shared pure selector, active-work lifecycle and revision "
"repository contracts; callers should be checked for preserving its "
"captured catalogue and pinned authority."
msgstr ""

